[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="Conversation" format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://game/dialogue/conversation.gd" id="1_convo"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_convo")
id = &"n4_choirc"
text = "# DRAFT
# Brother Piers on the east walk at dusk (night 4, fog). Background; dry.
# What the brothers say: the abbot's visitor, and the fast to starve it. If Thomas has named Simon (n4_thomas_simon):
# Thomas nursed Simon through a fever at Michaelmas, and Simon would do anything Thomas told him.
== start
(Brother Piers on the east walk, watching the fog fill the garth like milk in a bowl.)
Piers: You can't see the far walk. I keep thinking someone's standing in it.
-> topics

== again
Piers: Still foggy.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n4_choirc_talk] (Ask what the brothers are saying.) -> talk
* [if n4_thomas_simon] [if not n4_choirc_simon] (Ask about Brother Simon.) -> simon

== talk [set n4_choirc_talk]
Piers: That the abbot saw it at the foot of his bed. That it's hungry, and we fast so it finds nothing in us to eat.
(He doesn't smile.)
Piers: I'd sooner eat.
-> topics

== simon [set n4_choirc_simon]
Piers: Simon keeps to himself. Thomas nursed him through a fever at Michaelmas, and he's been Thomas's shadow since.
Piers: He'd walk into the river if Thomas told him it was good for his chest.
-> topics

== leave
Piers: Mind the fog, porter.
"
